  "curriculum": "The programme-specific 2026–2027 TER appendices I–IV govern the 180 EC bachelor. The eponymous Pharmacy major is the broad route with the required scientific and practice curriculum. It contains the common 60 EC first year, the 60 EC second year, 45 compulsory EC in Year 3 including the 15 EC research project, and 15 EC of restricted Pharmacy electives. The Medical Pharmaceutical Sciences major differs by substituting a 30 EC minor for the six Year 3 specialist courses. The degree has English and Dutch instruction. The TER identifies courses taught mainly in Dutch. The Safe Microbiological Techniques certificate is earned through Pharmaceutical Microbiology and adds no credits.",
  "progression": "Appendix IV requires Pharmaceutical Analysis before Bioanalysis and Instrumental Analysis. The cell practical and, where applicable, Physiology and Pharmacology or Biopharmacy 1 precede toxicology, microbiology, pharmacokinetics and Biopharmacy 2. Ocasys lists Microbiology and Biopharmacy 2 in paired rotation groups, so each is counted once, in separate teaching blocks. Molecules and Reactivity precedes the Organic Chemistry Practical. Physiology and Pharmacology and Receptor Pharmacology precede the Pharmacology Practical. In a valid nominal third year, complete the six required courses in the autumn, including enough early courses to exceed 130 EC four weeks before the Semester 2a project. Complete the 15 EC supervised project in 2a. A valid spread of restricted choices in the three separate 2b blocks is Advanced Human Disease Model Technologies, Pharmacology of Chronic Diseases and Ageing, and Herbal Medicine. This establishes feasible choice space without requiring those particular electives in the comparison.",
